<section class="runtime-section section-wrap" aria-labelledby="runtime-title">
  <div class="runtime-intro">
    <p class="section-kicker">ONE RETAINED RUNTIME</p>
    <h2 id="runtime-title">Describe the interface.<br />Keep the useful work.</h2>
    <p>
      Alicorn does not watch arbitrary application memory. Your code owns state and says when a
      change needs a new description. The runtime reconciles that description with retained
      identity and derived UI products.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/docs/concepts/retained-runtime">Read the runtime model <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </div>

  <div class="pipeline" aria-label="Alicorn runtime flow">
    <article class="pipeline-step">
      <span class="pipeline-overline">01 / AUTHOR</span>
      <h3>Odin app</h3>
      <p>State, control flow, keys, and UI descriptions stay in your program.</p>
      <span class="pipeline-code">ui.column · ui.text · ui.button</span>
    </article>
    <span class="pipeline-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    <article class="pipeline-step pipeline-step--active">
      <span class="pipeline-overline">02 / RETAIN</span>
      <h3>Alicorn runtime</h3>
      <p>Identity, input, semantics, layout, text, and paint are reconciled by change.</p>
      <span class="pipeline-code">describe → reconcile → present</span>
    </article>
    <span class="pipeline-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    <article class="pipeline-step">
      <span class="pipeline-overline">03 / PRESENT</span>
      <h3>Native host</h3>
      <p>The host owns the window, event loop, platform services, and GPU submission.</p>
      <span class="pipeline-code">SDL3 · SDL_GPU</span>
    </article>
  </div>

  <div class="runtime-rule">
    <span>APP STATE</span><b>→</b><span>EXPLICIT INVALIDATION</span><b>→</b><span>DEPENDENT WORK</span><b>→</b><span>NATIVE FRAME</span>
  </div>
</section>
